  "rationale": "The one home (SPEC_STANDARD 15.4) of every policy value Registry's generated code reads that is neither an environment setting (runtime_settings) nor an enumeration member or field type (models): typed constants of the data_provider module (State 3), which a consumer imports by name as the State 5 table 'Constants each module imports' lists (SPEC_STANDARD 6.10, 15.3.1, 15.9). Decided values are carried unchanged from the decisions in source_refs: A13's durations and refusal count, A18's 03:00, look and 30 x 24 hours, A19's 50 MB, A01's 128, A02's 40 (R0-90) and the characteristics' bounds, A17's 32 bytes, A09's rights and highest classes (rows in the enumeration values State 6 declares), A22's one type estimate by PresuPro. Technical values chosen by the author under the owner's delegation of 2026-11-11: the backup prefixes registry-backup- and registry-tmp- (neither begins with the other), the store's temporary suffix .new, STORE_VERSION 1 (the first store of re-authored Registry; the v1 store is not opened, the import reads a file), RELEASE_VERSION registry-2.0.0 and CONTRACT_VERSION registry-contract-2 (v1 being the first). OBJECT_FLOOR_AREA_MIN_EXCLUSIVE is a fixed-precision decimal written as a string (SPEC_STANDARD 15.4). A17's port bounds 1 and 65535 are LISTEN_PORT_MIN and LISTEN_PORT_MAX. Added in State 6 (State 2 round-68 T11 carried the backup key digest here): BACKUP_RECORD_VERSION 1 versions the record line a backup carries readable without its key; BACKUP_KEY_DIGEST_DOMAIN separates the key digest — sha256: and the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the domain's bytes, a zero byte and the key's UTF-8 bytes — from any other use of the key; BACKUP_KEY_DERIVATION_INFO is the HKDF-SHA256 info from which the AES-256-GCM key of a backup is derived. A new algorithm is a new record version, never a reinterpretation of an old one. A04 rule 6's six stages, which every refusal carries as its stage number (State 6 wire format), are six constants REFUSAL_STAGE_AUTHENTICATION 1 to REFUSAL_STAGE_LIFECYCLE 6 (owner, 2026-11-17): Refusal.stage stays an int, and a module names the stage it refuses at by the constant it imports. The first ordinals the design fixes as 1 have one home each (State 7 structure requests, 2026-11-17): REVISION_FIRST, the revision a Project or a Customer is made or imported with (State 1, 'an ordinal starting at 1'), and ACCESS_VERSION_FIRST, an agent session's access version at registration (A12 rule 1). Each later revision or version is one more than the one before; that step is what an ordinal is, not a value of its own. Added 2026-11-17 by the owner's decisions on the State 7 structure requests of operations, service_api and owner_interface: PERSONAL_DATA_FIELDS, the (answer model, field) pairs holding State 1's personal_data facts (A09 rule 4); SERVICE_AGENT_SESSION_HEADER, the header naming Kernel's agent session (R0-53); SERVICE_ANSWER_STATUS and REFUSAL_HTTP_STATUSES, v1's statuses (SOURCE.md L14: not_found 404, internal_error 500, every other code 422); UPLOAD_FORM_HEAD_MAX_BYTES, the bound of the multipart head an upload form sends before its file, its CSRF field first (A13 rule 5), 8192 a technical value delegated to the author. LISTENER_READ_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (30), how long a listener waits for a request's next bytes before closing the connection (State 2 round-90 T8, State 5 round-39 T3), a technical value delegated to the author. Added 2026-11-24 by the owner's decisions on the State 7 structure requests of owner_interface: OWNER_ACTIONS, one row of row model OwnerActionRoute for every OwnerAction member (total, keyed by the action), gives the method and path a request names it by and the two facts its admission needs: is_change, the actions A13 rule 2 calls changes of the session (showing a confirmation step, uploading a file, every submission, a sign-out), whose form carries the CSRF value, and touches_upload, the actions A16 rule 2 lists as reading or changing an uploaded file (an upload, showing the mapping, confirming the import, a sign-out); showing the confirmation step touches the uploaded file only when the action it confirms is the import, which is its confirm_action and not a fact of the action alone. Reads are GET and every other action POST; each path is the action's value after a slash, the project list's the root; no two rows share a method and a path. Sign-in is POST and no change: it carries no session and no CSRF value (A13 rule 4). A request whose method and path name no row names no action, and operations refuses it after stage (1) as a value outside its closed list, as the service API does an operation it does not know. OWNER_TARGET_PARAMETER is the query parameter that carries a request's target, an identity and never a personal value (R0-29); OWNER_CSRF_FIELD the form field, the upload's first multipart part included, that carries the CSRF value; OWNER_SESSION_COOKIE_NAME the session cookie's name, whose __Host- prefix makes a browser keep it only as Secure, for the whole of Registry's origin and for no other host (A13 rule 1; OWASP); it is set SameSite=Strict, so a browser never sends it with a request another site started (owner, 2026-11-24). Owner pages carry SERVICE_ANSWER_STATUS for an answer and the code's row of REFUSAL_HTTP_STATUSES for a refusal, one table for both surfaces. These are technical values chosen by the author under the owner's delegation. Added 2026-11-24 by the owner's decisions on the State 7 structure requests of operations and on the listener prototype of 2026-11-17: OWNER_AUDIT_ACTIONS, rows of row model OwnerAuditAction keyed by the owner action with, for marking a customer, its CustomerTransition and, for erasing a project, its ProjectErasure, gives the AuditAction M09 has an accepted owner action write (R0-58); an action with no row writes no entry. Answering an access request has the grant's row, and operations writes it only when the answer granted a project: a decline changes no session's projects and writes none (M09). LISTENER_CLOSE_DRAIN_SECONDS (2) and LISTENER_CLOSE_DRAIN_MAX_BYTES (64 MiB, more than an upload's IMPORT_FILE_MAX_BYTES with its framing) bound the staged close of a connection answered before its body was read to its end (RFC 9112 section 9.6): the listener shuts its writing side, reads and drops what the client still sends until either bound is reached or the client closes, then closes, so a client still sending receives the answer instead of a reset (prototype listener_proto, 2026-11-17). These are technical values chosen by the author under the owner's delegation. Added 2026-11-25 by A02 rule 1 (State 2 round-120 T16, round-121 T4; carried here by round-122 T1): WHITE_SPACE_CODE_POINTS, the white space set of a given value, exactly the 25 code points of Unicode's White_Space property A02 rule 1 lists (U+0009 to U+000D, U+0020, U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000 to U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000), each a one-character string in code point order; a string_tuple, since the readers test membership of the set and name no single member, and imported by given_values only (State 5 table). Added 2026-11-26 by the owner's decision on the State 7 round-01 topics of class B1 (protocol literals as constants): the protocol literals the notes wrote inline, each now with one home here and named by the notes as the imported constant. TEXT_ENCODING (utf-8, Python's codec name) is the one text encoding of every secret compared or measured in bytes, every JSON body and record line, every header value, form field and upload part decoded, and of the backup key digest's and derivation's inputs; TEXT_REPLACEMENT_CHARACTER (U+FFFD) replaces each byte of a header value that is no part of a valid sequence. CONTENT_TYPE_HEADER (Content-Type) and CONTENT_LENGTH_HEADER (Content-Length) are header names both surfaces read or write; SERVICE_AUTHORIZATION_HEADER (Authorization) and SERVICE_AUTHORIZATION_SCHEME (Bearer) carry a service's token (RFC 6750); SERVICE_ANSWER_CONTENT_TYPE (application/json; charset=utf-8) is the service answer's media type; SERVICE_INSTANT_UTC_MARK (Z) stands in place of an instant's UTC offset on the service wire. OWNER_COOKIE_HEADER (Cookie), OWNER_SET_COOKIE_HEADER (Set-Cookie) and OWNER_CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY_HEADER (Content-Security-Policy) are the owner interface's header names; OWNER_FORM_MEDIA_TYPE (application/x-www-form-urlencoded) is the media type of an owner form sent by POST. UPLOAD_FORM_MEDIA_TYPE (multipart/form-data), UPLOAD_BOUNDARY_PARAMETER (boundary) and UPLOAD_FILENAME_PARAMETER (filename) name an upload's media type and parameters (RFC 7578); UPLOAD_DELIMITER_PREFIX (a carriage return, a line feed and two hyphens) precedes the boundary in a part's delimiter and UPLOAD_CLOSE_SUFFIX (two hyphens, a carriage return and a line feed) follows the closing delimiter (RFC 2046 section 5.1.1). BACKUP_KEY_DIGEST_PREFIX (sha256:) begins the backup key digest and BACKUP_KEY_DIGEST_SEPARATOR (one zero character, one zero byte in TEXT_ENCODING) separates BACKUP_KEY_DIGEST_DOMAIN from the key in the digest's input, the digest described above. Each value is the one the notes already wrote; none is changed. Added 2026-11-26 by the owner's decision on the State 7 round-01 topics of class B2 (policy tables and sets as constants): the orders, sets and correspondences the notes wrote in prose, each now with one home here, values unchanged. PROJECT_VALUE_FAILURE_KINDS orders the RefusalKind values of the values stage of projects' operations (State 5 Errors of create_project, add_room and correct_project); AGENT_SESSION_FAILURE_KINDS orders the RefusalKind values of agent_sessions' owner operations as their State 5 Errors list them, not_granted and not_pending, which no one operation answers together, in the order RefusalKind declares them. CUSTOMER_ELIGIBILITY_REFUSALS maps a CustomerEligibility value other than eligible and unknown to the RefusalKind value a project's lifecycle stage answers for it. RUNTIME_SETTING_ORDER is the order in which load_configuration takes the RuntimeSettings field names within one check (A17 rule 2); RUNTIME_SETTINGS_REQUIRED the items each set, RUNTIME_SETTINGS_ALL_OR_NONE the four service tokens and the service API's address, all set or all unset, both in that order. STORE_COMPANION_SUFFIXES are the suffixes of the companion files SQLite may keep beside a database under its name, in the order a discarded store removes them (State 5, store.discard_new_store). OWNER_CHANGE_ACTIONS are the OwnerAction values operations runs in a writing transaction and SERVICE_CHANGE_OPERATIONS the ServiceOperation values it so runs for a service; they are not OWNER_ACTIONS' is_change, which is the CSRF value's rule (A13 rule 2) and also holds sign_out, upload_import and show_confirmation, which write no record. Added 2026-11-26 by the owner's decision on the State 7 round-01 topics of class B3 (each text form read in one place, given_values): REQUEST_ID_UNPRINTABLE_CATEGORIES, the Unicode general categories a request id may not hold, which make it not printable text (A01 rule 1) — control Cc, format Cf, surrogate Cs, private use Co and unassigned Cn, in the order the notes named them; a string_tuple of the categories' two-letter abbreviations, since check_request_id_form tests membership and names no single member. Added 2026-11-26 by the owner's decision on State 7 round-01 migration_import T18: DIGEST_ALGORITHM (sha256, the name Python's hashlib gives SHA-256) is the algorithm of the import file's digest and of the backup key's digest, each written as lowercase hexadecimal; BACKUP_KEY_DIGEST_PREFIX keeps its own value. The HKDF of a backup's key derivation is no digest of this kind and does not read it. Each value is the one the notes already wrote; none is changed. Added 2026-11-26 by the owner's decision on State 7 round-01 owner_interface T3 (a form path written and read in one place): OWNER_FORM_PATH_SEPARATOR (a full stop) stands between the parts of an owner form field's path, the names of OWNER_FORM_FIELDS included, as OWNER_FORM_POSITION_MARK stands in place of a tuple's position; the value is the one the notes already wrote.",
